messages:
li: Heads-up: found a confusing Android-only failure in the SDK samples. When uploading via Retrofit/OkHttp and using an Authenticator to refresh tokens, some devices showed duplicate or partial uploads after a connection recovery. Repro in sample app with ContentResolver stream. :thinking_face:
nora: that sounds like the non-repeatable RequestBody problem. Which client options are set?
li: default OkHttpClientBuilder except we accidentally left writeTimeout unset (0) and rely on retryOnConnectionFailure=true. Also followRedirects=true. Authenticator is synchronous and returns a rebuilt request with new Authorization header. snippet:
```java
Authenticator auth = (route, response) -> {
  synchronized (lock) {
    if (refreshing) return null;
    refreshing = true;
    try {
      String t = tokenRefresher.refreshBlocking();
      return response.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer "+t).build();
    } finally { refreshing = false; }
  }
};
```
aditya: OkHttp will try to recover certain connection failures and will re-create requests using call.clone(). If the RequestBody reads from a one-shot InputStream (ContentResolver/FileDescriptor), it can't be replayed. Result: duplicate packets or partial writes depending on timing.
li: saw it mostly on API 21-24 devices and when the server responded with 302->401 in redirect chain or connection reset. Also saw some ANRs because writeTimeout was infinite.
nora: short-term mitigations we tried: 1) set writeTimeout to a finite value; 2) retryOnConnectionFailure(false) for upload endpoints; 3) make RequestBody repeatable by writing to cache file or byte[]; 4) move refresh out of Authenticator to an Interceptor that surfaces 401 so the caller can re-submit with a repeatable body.
aditya: code helper we added to samples to make a file-backed body:
```java
static RequestBody toFileRequestBody(InputStream in, MediaType mt, Context ctx) throws IOException {
  File tmp = File.createTempFile("rw-upload-", ".tmp", ctx.getCacheDir());
  try (OutputStream os = new FileOutputStream(tmp)) {
    byte[] buf = new byte[8192];
    int r;
    while ((r = in.read(buf)) != -1) os.write(buf,0,r);
  }
  return RequestBody.create(mt, tmp);
}
```
aditya: tradeoffs: disk + latency vs safety. Prefer resumable/chunked uploads if caller can.
li: for samples we'll add toggles: useFileBacking=true, retryOnConnectionFailure=false, followRedirects=false for upload flows, and sensible writeTimeout/readTimeout. Also add an instrumented test that simulates connection reset + 401 to ensure only one upload attempt hits the fake server.
nora: SDK docs should include an "Uploads on mobile" section: explain non-repeatable body issues, authenticators vs interceptors, timeout defaults, and recommend chunked uploads. Also consider adding a runtime warning when a non-repeatable body is used while an Authenticator is registered.
aditya: small runtime warning added in sample wrapper: if (client.authenticator()!=null && !isRepeatable(request.body())) log.warn("Authenticator + non-repeatable body may cause duplicate uploads");
sdk-bot: Created issue #4217: "android-sdk: prevent duplicate streaming uploads when using Authenticator + OkHttp retries" https://github.com/redwood-inference/android-samples/issues/4217 :robot_face:
li: I'll open a PR with the temp-file helper, docs blurb, sample toggle, and the instrumented test. Tagging @nora @aditya for review. Thanks :thumbsup:
